[
    {
        "content": "<p>I just ran into something weird over at <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38227\">#38227</a>. That PR is intended to be purely a stylistic cleanup, with the only change made to theorems being indirect via a <code>variable</code> block. But somehow this broke three different proofs in one of the test files. Does anyone have any idea of what's going on?</p>",
        "id": 591812924,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1777472785
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><img alt=\"image.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"605x67\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/YrwBmEIi2YMgne1PDGD7j4iz/image.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/YrwBmEIi2YMgne1PDGD7j4iz/image.png/840x560.webp\"><br>\nThese are the failing tests, so maybe it's something to do with <code>add_le_add_left</code>? I'm not sure.</p>",
        "id": 591813284,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1777472831
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>bound</code> is an interface to <code>aesop</code> so I wouldn't expect any sensitivity to the order of hypotheses. Very surprising.</p>\n<p>Maybe you can try bisection? Apply only half your changes, see if <code>bound</code> still fails. If it does, again halve the changes. If a set of changes makes <code>bound</code> continue to work, the problem must be in the other half, so try only applying that half and halving it further. Repeat until <code>bound</code> fails.</p>",
        "id": 591814728,
        "sender_full_name": "Anne Baanen",
        "timestamp": 1777473135
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The test file is 2,000 imports deep. But I guess I have two hours to kill.</p>",
        "id": 591814864,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1777473160
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe I am being paranoid, but <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38467\">#38467</a> was recently merged.</p>",
        "id": 591815029,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1777473197
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, I did make some existing theorems into aliases.</p>",
        "id": 591815225,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1777473237
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>When looking at it, one of the concerns was publicity of aliases and I noticed that there were 4 private <code>bound</code> aliases.</p>",
        "id": 591815331,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1777473257
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I am only mentioning this since this is a <code>bound</code> issue right after this change.  I don't really expect this to be the culprit, but... who knows!</p>",
        "id": 591815456,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1777473286
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'll try and revert that in my branch and see if anything happens.</p>",
        "id": 591815805,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1777473371
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you are not using <code>alias_in</code>, I would be very surprised if that affected you.</p>",
        "id": 591816035,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1777473426
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Good/bad news: this wasn't the culprit</p>",
        "id": 591819104,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1777474128
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Time to bisect</p>",
        "id": 591819351,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1777474189
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Finally got around to bisecting. The good news is that I managed to isolate the exact line that causes the error. The bad news is I have no idea why it causes the error.</p>",
        "id": 595474570,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1778928816
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39413\">#39413</a></p>",
        "id": 595474571,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1778928817
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The error is a consequence of changing a theorem to an alias?  Am I understanding correctly?</p>",
        "id": 595475701,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1778929670
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yep</p>",
        "id": 595475765,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1778929710
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think that aliases are indexed differently than theorems so it could be that <code>bound</code> \"misses\" aliases.</p>",
        "id": 595475827,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1778929743
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is the theorem tagged as <code>bound</code> somewhere, though?</p>",
        "id": 595475855,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1778929765
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>not that i can tell, oddly enough</p>",
        "id": 595475876,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1778929780
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>couldn't find the additive version tagged either</p>",
        "id": 595475904,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1778929794
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>but maybe i missed something?</p>",
        "id": 595475908,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1778929798
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Can you use this information to write an <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a>?</p>",
        "id": 595476076,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1778929905
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't know how I'm supposed to write a mwe when the error is changing an existing theorem</p>",
        "id": 595476240,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1778930039
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>bound</code> internally uses <code>aesop</code>, so it might be also some <code>aesop</code> tagging that changes the behaviour.  <span aria-label=\"shrug\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f937\" role=\"img\" title=\"shrug\">:shrug:</span></p>",
        "id": 595478227,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1778931460
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a chance I just stumbled across nondeterminism? And that making this theorem an alias is somehow changing an internal key that makes this theorem not fire in time, or whatnot.</p>",
        "id": 595552617,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1778979124
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>From what I can tell <code>bound</code> is somehow getting stuck on unsolveable goals </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Error</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MathlibTest</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Bound</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">bound</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">102</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">42</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"n\">aesop'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failed</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">prove</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">after</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exhaustive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">search</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Initial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goal</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Remaining</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goals</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">after</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">safe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rules</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hbc</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ha</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
